@@ -313,6 +313,13 @@ state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transi
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
 again.
 
+In command mode, `TerminalUi` supports focused-pane visual selections. `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` start
+character, line, and block visual modes for the focused pane; `h/j/k/l` and arrow keys move the
+selection cursor. `y` yanks the active selection, `Y` yanks a line selection, and command-mode `Y`
+yanks the current line. Yanks are emitted as OSC 52 terminal clipboard sequences during rendering and
+also stored in UI state for harness assertions. `Esc`, pane changes, chat sends, prompt entry, and
+other modal transitions cancel the active visual selection.
+
 `src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:
 
 - `UiMode`, `PaneFocus`, `UiSurface`, `UiKey`, and `UiAction` model terminal interactions.
